counterexample_dsp:
Create two t1 rows (A and B).
Let both of them share the c2 value X in t5, but give A an extra private value Y and B an extra private value Z.  Thus:
  A → {X , Y}
  B → {X , Z}
The sets overlap but neither is a subset of the other.  Q2 sees the common value X and outputs (A , B) (and (B , A)); Q1 outputs nothing because the subset condition fails both ways.

