INSERT INTO t5 (c1, c2, c3) VALUES ('B', 'z', 2.00);

counterexample_dsp:
Two t1 keys A and B.  Give them one common c2 (x).  Give A another c2 (y) that B does not have, and give B yet another c2 (z) that A does not have:
  A → {x,y}
  B → {x,z}
Now set(A) is NOT a subset of set(B), so Q1 returns nothing, but Q2, which only needs one shared c2 (x) and some extra c2 for B (z), will return the pair (A,B) (and symmetrically (B,A)).

